Date: Sat, 9 May 2026 22:17:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?P09.46-B5b:=20class-aware=20assists=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20find=20overriders=20+=20implement=20override=20+=20base-awar?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20constructor?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three IDE assists building on B.4b (inheritance) and B.4c (methods):

1. Find all overriders (ide): new navigation entry mirroring "Go to
   implementation" but specialized to the rustcc class chain. Given a
   method declared inside a `class Foo { ... }` body, walks all classes
   in the crate and surfaces same-named methods on descendants. Lives
   in crates/ide/src/find_class_overriders.rs.

2. Implement override (ide-assists): on a cursor inside `class Dog :
   Animal { ... }`, walks ancestors via `hir::Class::ancestors`, lists
   methods not yet overridden in `Dog`, and offers one assist per
   missing method that inserts a stub `fn` with a `todo!()` body.
   Mirrors `add_missing_impl_members`'s shape.

3. Generate constructor for class — base-aware extension: when the
   class has a `: Base` clause and Sema resolves it, the existing
   `generate_class_new` now flattens base fields into the param list,
   produces a `__base: Base::new(...)` initializer, and only
   shorthand-initializes this class's own fields.

Wiring this required teaching the Sema source-to-def layer about
class containers:

  * `ChildContainer::ClassId` arm + `ChildBySource for ClassId`
    walking `ClassItems::of` so `Sema::to_def(&ast::Fn)` resolves a
    function declared inside a class body.
  * `container_to_def` Item::Class arm routing CLASS_MEMBER_LIST
    children into `ChildContainer::ClassId`.
  * `analyze_impl` Class arm building a SourceAnalyzer keyed off
    `GenericDefId::AdtId(AdtId::ClassId(_))`.
  * `hir::Class::base_class`, `ancestors`, `items`, `all_in_crate`
    helpers exposed to IDE callers.

Test counts:
  ide-assists: 2764 (was 2757, +7)
  ide:         1297 (was 1292, +5)
  ide-completion: 729 (unchanged)
  hir-def:     481, hir-ty: 972 (unchanged)

